{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01HnmFr7sq2zVbqdMa8Kdbfj","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/fm_per_100k.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"fm\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Read census data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Get total farmers markets\nfm_total = fm.aggregate(total_fm=fm.farmers_markets.sum())\n\n# Get US total population for 2025\nus_pop = census.filter(census.SUMLEV == 10).select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\")\n\n# Join them with a constant key and calculate the metric\nfm_total_k = fm_total.mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\nus_pop_k = us_pop.mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\nexpr = (\n    fm_total_k.join(us_pop_k, fm_total_k.k == us_pop_k.k)\n      .mutate(fm_per_100k=fm_total_k.total_fm / us_pop_k.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_fm\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"fm_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see:\n1. The census data with SUMLEV=10 gives us the U.S. total population of 341,784,857 for 2025 (POPESTIMATE2025)\n2. The farmers_markets data has a column called \"farmers_markets\" with state-by-state counts\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Sum all farmers_markets from all states\n2. Use the US total population from census\n3. Calculate the ratio: (total farmers_markets / population) * 100,000\n\nLet me write a build script to do this join and calculate the metric.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I'll create a build script to join the two tables and calculate the metric:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01HnmFr7sq2zVbqdMa8Kdbfj","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/fm_per_100k.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"fm\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Read census data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Get total farmers markets\nfm_total = fm.aggregate(total_fm=fm.farmers_markets.sum())\n\n# Get US total population for 2025\nus_pop = census.filter(census.SUMLEV == 10).select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\")\n\n# Join them with a constant key and calculate the metric\nfm_total_k = fm_total.mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\nus_pop_k = us_pop.mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\nexpr = (\n    fm_total_k.join(us_pop_k, fm_total_k.k == us_pop_k.k)\