{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786914538930},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Calculate how many farmers markets the U.S. has per 100,000 residents\n2. Use a farmers markets dataset and a census file\n3. Provide the answer to four decimal places\n4. Use tools to do any math necessary\n5. Only mention verified facts\n\nLet me follow the xorq analyst procedure:\n1. **Orient** - Check if there are semantic models and existing aliases\n2. **Ingest** - If needed, ingest the datasets into the catalog\n3. **Compute** - Use xorq_select to get values\n4. **Declare** - Create obligations for verification\n5. **Verify** - Run xorq_verify to confirm\n6. **Check lineage** - Verify sources are legitimate\n\nLet me start by orienting to the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents using a verified approach. Let me start by orienting to the catalog and then ingesting these datasets."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01VbUYfTPRMDnVRhadjvhCMM","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_014v87MpEnHUFQPvDdeh2PzH","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":342,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8149,"totalTokens":8501,"cost":{"input":0.000009999